From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:21:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Recheck cross-document new children in
 ReplaceChild(VectorOf<Node>)

FlyWeb next batch: from branch-heads/8078 40bf5125f6. Applied after seguridad/siguiente/chromium/0004; applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Recheck cross-document new children in ReplaceChild(VectorOf<Node>)
>
> In ContainerNode::ReplaceChild(const VectorOf<Node>&, ...), removing
> the old child can run synchronous event handlers (e.g. a fieldset
> blurring its focused, disabled control). The DOMTreeMutationDetector
> used around that removal only watches the old child's and parent's
> document, so if a handler inserted one of the new children into a
> different document, the structural recheck was skipped and the node was
> linked into two child lists, corrupting the DOM tree.
>
> This CL forces the recheck when any of the new children is not in this
> node's document.
>
